[[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/free5gc/issues/comments/619601378","html_url":"https://github.com/free5gc/free5gc/issues/23#issuecomment-619601378","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/free5gc/issues/23","id":619601378,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDYxOTYwMTM3OA==","user":{"login":"free5gc-org","id":60502770,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwNTAyNzcw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60502770?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/free5gc-org","html_url":"https://github.com/free5gc-org","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/free5gc-org/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/free5gc-org/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/free5gc-org/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/free5gc-org/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/free5gc-org/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/free5gc-org/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/free5gc-org/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/free5gc-org/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/free5gc-org/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-04-26T18:29:52Z","updated_at":"2020-04-26T18:29:52Z","body":"Hi,\r\nFor the first question, why are two different function used in this case?\r\nin general, AMF should use amfUeNgapID to find the UE context,\r\nbut in our implementation, use ranUeNgapID or amfUeNgapID is ok to find the same UE context.\r\nSo this is not the real reason for the error.\r\n\r\nAnd why is the Test throwing this error when run for the second time?\r\nBecause we hard code some data in our test, e.g amfUeNgapID of UE. If you run the test for second time without restarting the CN, the state of CN will mismatch the test data, and the test will fail.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/free5gc/issues/comments/619601378/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/free5gc/issues/comments/619619750","html_url":"https://github.com/free5gc/free5gc/issues/23#issuecomment-619619750","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/free5gc/issues/23","id":619619750,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDYxOTYxOTc1MA==","user":{"login":"endrigoshi","id":32163632,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMTYzNjMy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32163632?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/endrigoshi","html_url":"https://github.com/endrigoshi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/endrigoshi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/endrigoshi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/endrigoshi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/endrigoshi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/endrigoshi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/endrigoshi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/endrigoshi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/endrigoshi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/endrigoshi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-04-26T20:24:40Z","updated_at":"2020-04-26T20:24:40Z","body":"Hi again!\r\n\r\nThank you for the detailed answer. \r\n\r\nHowever, since you said that both `amfUeNgapID` and `ranUeNgapID` can be used, what is then the reason that `amf_context.AMF_Self().RanUeFindByAmfUeNgapID(aMFUENGAPID.Value)` returns `nil` and `ran.RanUeFindByRanUeNgapID(rANUENGAPID.Value)` doesn't?\r\n\r\nOne more thing that I would like to add is that the Test does PASS, but I can see the following Error in the AMF side. And I would also like to note that the Registration procedure works with no Error. The error is seen when the functions performing Deregistration are called.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/free5gc/issues/comments/619619750/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/free5gc/issues/comments/621875992","html_url":"https://github.com/free5gc/free5gc/issues/23#issuecomment-621875992","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/free5gc/issues/23","id":621875992,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDYyMTg3NTk5Mg==","user":{"login":"free5gc-org","id":60502770,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwNTAyNzcw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60502770?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/free5gc-org","html_url":"https://github.com/free5gc-org","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/free5gc-org/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/free5gc-org/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/free5gc-org/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/free5gc-org/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/free5gc-org/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/free5gc-org/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/free5gc-org/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/free5gc-org/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/free5gc-org/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-04-30T14:08:16Z","updated_at":"2020-04-30T14:08:16Z","body":"Hi,\r\nFirst, our AMF assign amfUeNgapID from 1, 2, 3, ... (increase 1 every time)\r\nAs mentioned earlier, our test just use fake data in the test, so the fake ue context always has amfUeNgapID = 1, that means it won't update amfUeNgapID no matter how the core network assign amfUeNgapID\r\nyou can check the test code here:\r\nhttps://github.com/free5gc/free5gc/blob/ecb48718062ecfd3f53715219ba1746d147b62ca/src/test/registration_test.go#L117\r\non the other hand, ranUeNgapID is assigned by fake ran, so AMF can update UE's ranUeNgapID correctly, then use ranUeNgapID to find the UE, but fake ran didn't update UE's amfUeNgapID which is assigned by AMF.\r\n\r\nIf you don't restart CN and run the test for second time, AMF will assign this ue with amfUeNgapID = 2 (amfUeNgapID 1 has assigned in the previous test), but remember that in the test, the fake ue always has amfUeNgapID = 1, so AMF cannot find the UE by amfUeNgapID.\r\n\r\nIn fact, if you trace our test code, you will find that we just utilize \"go test\" command to run our test, and we did not check the output of the core network. The \"pass test\" message is reported by go testing package, not by us. So the correct way to check the test pass or not is to see if there is any error log in the terminal. Just ignore \"pass\" message reported by go testing package","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/free5gc/issues/comments/621875992/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/free5gc/issues/comments/622453674","html_url":"https://github.com/free5gc/free5gc/issues/23#issuecomment-622453674","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/free5gc/issues/23","id":622453674,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDYyMjQ1MzY3NA==","user":{"login":"endrigoshi","id":32163632,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMTYzNjMy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32163632?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/endrigoshi","html_url":"https://github.com/endrigoshi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/endrigoshi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/endrigoshi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/endrigoshi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/endrigoshi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/endrigoshi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/endrigoshi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/endrigoshi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/endrigoshi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/endrigoshi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-05-01T16:16:24Z","updated_at":"2020-05-01T16:16:24Z","body":"Thank you! The explanation was really helpful!\r\nI’m closing the issue now.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/free5gc/free5gc/issues/comments/622453674/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]]